<title>UK: Ibstock profits fall on weak housing, pulp.</title>
<headline>Ibstock profits fall on weak housing, pulp.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to June 30</p>
<p>			   (million stg unless stated)</p>
<p> Shr (pence)		0.87		   vs 3.78</p>
<p> Dividend (pence)	 0.75		   vs 0.75</p>
<p> Pretax		     2.4		    vs 14.0</p>
<p> Turnover		   115.1		  vs 122.1</p>
<p>NOTE - The building materials and forest products group Ibstock Plc said first-half results were affected by low paper pulp prices and a weak housing market but said the general outlook for the UK brick market is &quot;improving.&quot;</p>
</text>
